Figure 2 illustrates the in vivo kinetics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, demonstrating their retention at the injection site and gradual clearance over time. Whole-mouse imaging (A) shows that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 remains confined to the calf muscle injection sites for up to 21 days, without apparent distribution to internal organs, as confirmed by ex vivo imaging of dissected organs (B). Quantification of fluorescence intensity (C) reveals a rapid decrease in signal after day 0, a transient increase on day 2, followed by a steady decline, with approximately 20% of the initial signal remaining at day 21. This indicates Nano-11 is cleared locally without systemic accumulation.